- [Alternate gametes]{color=#800080} have exactly 100% of the genome; but the chromosomes might be scrambled

=== layout: bookend

# Key Takeaways

@body

- Translocation heterozygotes form a four-chromosome pairing.
- The segregation pattern determines the chromosome pairs.
- Alternate segregation produces balanced products.
- Adjacent segregation produces duplication/deletion products.

